            # (1 unchanged attribute hidden)
        }

Azure API Schema Check:
Queried Azure API schema for the enable field:
  Resource: Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines@2024-03-01
  Path: body.properties.scheduledEventsProfile.osImageNotificationProfile.enable
  Expected Type: Bool

Analysis:
- Azure API expects Bool type (confirmed via schema query)
- Module sends boolean value: enable = true (line 427 of migrate_main.tf)
- Azure API returns string value: "true"
- This creates perpetual drift on every terraform plan

Root Cause:
This appears to be an Azure API serialization issue where the API accepts Bool but returns
string. The module needs to be fixed to send string "true"/"false" instead of boolean 
true/false to match what Azure API returns.

Fix Required:
Update migrate_main.tf line 427 and 430:
  OLD: enable = true
  NEW: enable = "true"
  
  OLD: enable = false  
  NEW: enable = "false"

Test Result: FAILED
- Step 3 shows unacceptable persistent drift
- Test cannot proceed to Step 4 without fixing this module bug
